abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. Every two-connected graph with at most five Steinerberger boundary vertices has diameter at most two, and the connected graphs with exactly five boundary vertices are the bridge subdivisions of 227 reduced graphs of order at most fourteen, answering Problem 6.1 of Chiem, Dudarov, Lee, Lee and Liu. Connected graphs of maximum degree three with six boundary vertices are the bridge subdivisions of 201 reduced graphs. For n >= 6 every two-tree on n vertices has at least ceil(n/2)+2 boundary vertices; the extremal two-trees are classified and counted exactly. Lean proves the degree-three obstruction, the local certificate systems and further components. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
